    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at this NDA for a new fintech client and I'm a bit stuck on the 'residuals' part. Can you explain what this section actually means for me? \n\n'Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Receiving Party shall be free to use for any purpose the residuals resulting from access to or use of the Confidential Information, provided that the Receiving Party shall not disclose such residuals.' \n\nDoes this mean I can still use general coding patterns or logic I pick up while working with them for my other clients, or am I strictly blocked from using anything I learned there?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
